The page keys are where the Japanese kana keys were (specials 0-2 of the Japanese layout, its crops and rollovers: Back and OK are specials 3 and 4 in the US too), the current page's key lit in the highlight colour (6, the dialogue's names); L1 / R1 turn the page as well. The label row is the title, the three page keys and Back / OK: in English in the keyboard's 12-pixel cells, in Spanish in pieces at the original font's cells (NAMING_LABEL_PIECES). The player's and the partner's keyboard are the same box.

The mod font gets 27 glyphs (F06C-F087: â ê î ô û ä ë ö ã õ ì ù ß, their capitals but ß, ♥ ★; tools/font/extra.txt and b.txt), font_extra.h and font_b.h regenerated. The memory card's title maps every mod glyph to a plain Shift-JIS letter or symbol (PLAIN_LETTERS: F040-F087, F07F skipped; ♥ a white star).

